> JPY (Japanese yen) -> ru'urjupuje

It's interesting that the ISO chose this code, because modern Japanese
never pronounce their currency as "yen"; they pronounce it as "en",
meaning "round object" (=E5=86=86), since it was modelled on the circular
Spanish dollar coins. Some historical details are here:
http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yen#Pronunciation_and_etymology

